SUMMARY:Dumpling Making Workshop with Lani Chan at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 3-hour hands-on dumpling workshop led by Lani Chan\, founder of Hei Ma\, where you’ll learn to make dumplings entirely from scratch — wrappers\, fillings\, and all. You’ll start by making the dough. From there\, you’ll form and cook vegetarian dumplings\, learn to make scallion pancakes\, and pair everything with Hei Ma chili crisp and a special dipping sauce made with Gold Ridge Organic Farms Apple Cider Balsamic Vinegar. \nThe experience begins with a ride aboard our apple-themed trolley out to the Apple Cottage\, where the class will take place surrounded by the beauty of the farm. Each guest will receive an apple-blossom pink apron to take home and enjoy a refreshing citrus shrub alongside their freshly made dumplings. Whether you’re a seasoned home cook or a first-time dumpling maker\, this is an experience you won’t forget — good food\, great company\, and a deeper connection to the ingredients grown right here in Sonoma County. \nLani Chan is the co-founder of Hei Ma (formerly known as Big Spoon Sauce Co.)\, a Sonoma County-based small-batch sauce brand rooted in Chinese culinary tradition and peak-season California produce. What began as a chili crisp project in a Brooklyn apartment in 2019 has grown into a community-driven food brand celebrated for its bold flavors and cultural heart.
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/dumpling-making-workshop-with-lani-chan-at-gold-ridge-organic-farms/
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms\, 3387 Canfield Rd\, Sebastopol\, 95472
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2F94515C-0B09-4754-A648-EAF18E5B50D3.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Gold Ridge Organic Farms":MAILTO:info@goldridgeorganicfarms.com
END:VEVENT
